    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Silliness.</strong> Life is too short to not be full of laughter. I generally find most parts of life are worth taking seriously, and therefore worth beign able to laugh at. Being able to laugh easily together is important to survive <a href="https://waitbutwhy.com/2014/02/pick-life-partner-part-2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">20,000 Wednesdays</a> together.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Physical affection.</strong> Touch means a lot to me. I&rsquo;m a sexual creature and feel a deep sense of love and connection through physical contact, in all forms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Someone physically active who likes to spend time outside.</strong> I&rsquo;m someone who is endlessly fascinated by virtual worlds and strategy video games, books, Wikipedia, etc., and can easily spend time in front of the computer. As such, I&rsquo;ve discovered that it&rsquo;s best if my partner has a natural drive towards the sunlight, towards movement, and being fit. I really like all of those things myself, and it works best if I&rsquo;m not the only one in the partnership initiating outdoors adventures. Bonus points if we can delight in games together too.
